  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_011CgFzmpZUsoks4b62wJK1N:0",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": "Octopuses are remarkable marine animals with three hearts, blue blood, and eight arms lined with suckers. Each arm contains a large share of the animal's neurons, so an arm can taste, touch, and even react on its own."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_011CgFzmpZUsoks4b62wJK1N:0",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Their skin is packed with chromatophores, tiny pigment sacs that let them change color and texture in a fraction of a second."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_011CgFzmpZUsoks4b62wJK1N:0",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " This camouflage helps them blend into rocks and coral, and some species can even mimic other animals, such as venomous sole or sea snakes."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_011CgFzmpZUsoks4b62wJK1N:0",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Octopuses are also highly intelligent and curious, and they can solve puzzles, open jars, and recognize individual humans. Most species live only one to two years, and females often die soon after their eggs hatch."
    }
  },
  {
    "kind": "text.chunk",
    "payload": {
      "streamId": "msg_011CgFzmpZUsoks4b62wJK1N:0",
      "channel": "text",
      "text": " Their short lives and sharp minds make them a fascinating puzzle for biologists studying how intelligence can evolve outside the mammal line."
    }
  },
